Create a `writeErrorJSON` helper (can go in the existing `json_helpers.go` if it exists, or a new file):
```go
func writeErrorJSON(w http.ResponseWriter, status int, message string) {
    w.Header().Set("Content-Type", "application/json")
    w.WriteHeader(status)
    resp := map[string]any{"error": message, "status": status}
    if err := json.NewEncoder(w).Encode(resp); err != nil {
        slog.Warn("json encode error response failed", "error", err)
    }
}
```

Update dashboard `api.ts` error handling to try JSON parse first, fall back to text:
```typescript
if (!res.ok) {
    const text = await res.text();
    let message = text;
    try {
        const json = JSON.parse(text);
        message = json.error || text;
    } catch {}
    throw new Error(message || `Request failed (${res.status})`);
}
```
